commit f5ca39a5f181ba09ec1fef444e8bfb92d501d532

C03: «dime si …» after a conjunction is the same indirect question; with Steam open, an installed question about a game reads its manifests (APPS1613)

H0275 «Abre Steam y dime si Fall Guys ya está instalado» never resolved: the NETWORK1293 reading of «decime si …» as an indirect question applied only at the start of the request, so after «y» the «si» was taken for a condition and the unsupported-deferred-effect veto refused the whole compound; resolved by hand, its second clause went to the Start catalog (app.installed) although the person had just opened Steam and asked about a game. Now «dime/decime/contame/fijate/tell me si|if|whether» is the indirect question after a conjunction or a clause boundary too; inside a compound that opened Steam, an installed question about a name absent from the Start catalog decides game.installed.named, whose title and provider are read from the clause itself (installed_game_title, installed_game_provider); «decime», «contame» and «fijate» join the observation heads. Registry-wide diff: H0275 (plan app.open + game.installed.named) and H0221 «decime qué onda con el wifi» (wifi.status, the same read that covered it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


